Tell iOS what a field holds: TextInputConfiguration's autofill hint as `textContentType`.

Ported from flutter/flutter engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/darwin/ios/framework/Source/FlutterTextInputPlugin.mm
@ 3.50.1 (ae9b586f34a8443573f82ef57c3bf914a908cbf7): `ToUITextContentType` and `configureWithDictionary:`'s
`textContentType`. Copyright 2014 The Flutter Authors. BSD-3-Clause.

What: GPUITextInputView's `textContentType` maps GPUI's `AutofillHint` through Flutter's table (by Flutter's hint
names: username, password, newPassword, oneTimeCode, email, telephoneNumber, name, fullStreetAddress, postalCode,
creditCardNumber), and no hint to "", Flutter's value for a field without autofill, which turns iOS's autofill off.
The view had no content type, so iOS offered no password, one-time-code or contact autofill.

Why: patch 0005 added the hint; Android (Parallax) and the web (patch 0034) already read it.

Test: patch 0028's table gains testDisablingAutofillOnInputClient and a row checking every GPUI hint against UIKit's
constant, on the iOS simulator (`scripts/ios-text-oracle.sh` in Parallax).

Upstream PR: not filed yet (needs 0005 upstream first).

diff --git a/gpui-pre-ios/src/ios/text_input.rs b/gpui-pre-ios/src/ios/text_input.rs
